---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How AviKaiDo handles contact-form, chat, and email inquiries."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="section__eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="answer">
        AviKaiDo collects only the information you choose to send through our contact form, live
        chat, or email so we can respond to your inquiry. We do not sell personal data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 42rem;">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Name, work email, company, role, message content, and optional timeline preference when
        you submit the contact form or email {SITE_EMAIL}. Live chat may also collect messages and
        basic device/browser data needed to operate the widget.
      </p>
      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        To reply to your request, schedule discovery conversations, create CRM records, and
        maintain ordinary business records (including invoicing for clients). Contact-form
        submissions are processed by <strong>Zoho CRM</strong>. Live chat / visitor engagement is
        processed by <strong>Zoho SalesIQ</strong> when enabled. Client invoicing uses
        <strong>Zoho Books / Zoho Invoice</strong>. Email replies are sent from Gmail
        ({SITE_EMAIL}).
      </p>
      <h2>Processors</h2>
      <p>
        Zoho Corporation and its regional data centers act as processors for CRM, chat, and
        billing tools. See Zoho’s privacy documentation for their practices. Gmail (Google) is
        used for business email.
      </p>
      <h2>Retention &amp; contact</h2>
      <p>
        Inquiry and CRM records are kept as long as needed for follow-up and ordinary business
        records. Questions about your data: email
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
